// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dnd/magicitems.js — the magic items of the System Reference Document 5.2
// (CC BY 4.0), by their SRD 5.2 names, as data for real-time play.
//
// The contract is notes/alpha3-data-spec.md ("Magic items"). Every entry has
// name, rarity, attune, slot, art, cols [main, dark, light] and desc (what it
// does in this game), plus effect fields:
//   weapons  base, plus, extra [n, d, type], extraVs { types, dice }, vorpal, keen,
//            returning, light, slayer
//   armour   armorSet, plus, resist         shields  shieldPlus        ammo  ammo, plus, extra
//   worn     wear: { ac, save, saves, skills, adv, resist, immune, setAb, ab, speed, jump, fly,
//            flyDur, waterBreathing, swim, darkvision, spellDC, spellAttack, regen, invisible,
//            featherFall, climb, carry, light, truesight, noSleep, freedom, luck, hp, prof }
//   use      cast / castList + charges (+ recharge: 'dawn', castLvl), drink, bag, summonMob (+ n)
//   other    curse: '...' (the downside), todo: '...' (what the game can't do yet)
//
// Families with a version per weapon or armour (Weapon +1, Armor of Resistance,
// Flame Tongue, Vorpal Sword...) are one generic entry; the game rolls the actual
// weapon or armour when it drops:
//   base:     'any' (any simple or martial weapon), 'any_sword', 'any_axe', 'any_blade' (slashing),
//             'any_bludgeon', 'any_ranged', or a DND_WEAPONS key / 'longbow' / 'shortbow'
//   armorSet: 'any', 'any_light_armor', 'any_medium_armor', 'any_heavy_armor', or an armour key
// Families with a version per damage type, giant, dragon, gem or creature type
// (Potion of Resistance, Belt of Giant Strength, Dragon Scale Mail, Ioun Stone,
// Ammunition of Slaying...) have one entry each, so the effect is concrete.
//
// Notes on values:
//   - extraVs dice with no type ([3, 6]) deal the weapon's own damage type.
//   - adv uses skill keys (DND_SKILLS), '<ab>_save', 'charm', 'fear', 'poison',
//     'initiative' and 'spells' (saving throws against spells and magical effects).
//   - immune uses damage types and conditions ('poison', 'charm', 'fear', 'disease').
//   - summonMob uses SRD 5.2 creature names in snake_case; drink without dur is permanent
//     (manuals and tomes).
// Spell scrolls are generated by the game for every spell, so none are listed here.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

